Extracted 2026-07-29 from github.com/rudizee007/spt-txn-x402-solana, preserving
commit history. These packages are chain-agnostic and depend on nothing outside
the Go standard library; the dependency direction runs from chain-specific
consumers to this module and never back.

Enforcement points are intentionally free and open: running one should cost
nothing. The commercial boundary is operating a fleet of them and proving
compliance with them — control plane, aggregation, retention, control mappings.
Security features are never gated.

Specification: draft-coetzee-oauth-spt-txn-tokens-03
  https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-coetzee-oauth-spt-txn-tokens/
Reference implementation: https://github.com/rudizee007/spt-txn-poc

No third-party dependencies. No copyleft (GPL/LGPL/MPL) code is present.

STATUS: proof of concept. Not externally audited. Not for production use.
